.TH EXP 3 "May 2026" "Substrate" "Library Functions Manual"
.SH NAME
exp, expf, expl, exp2, exp2f, exp2l, expm1, expm1f, expm1l,
exp10, exp10f, exp10l, exp10m1, exp2m1 \- exponential functions
.SH LIBRARY
Math library (libm, \-lm)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include <math.h>
.PP
.BI "double exp(double " x );
.br
.BI "float expf(float " x );
.br
.BI "long double expl(long double " x );
.PP
.BI "double exp2(double " x );
.br
.BI "float exp2f(float " x );
.br
.BI "long double exp2l(long double " x );
.PP
.BI "double expm1(double " x );
.br
.BI "float expm1f(float " x );
.br
.BI "long double expm1l(long double " x );
.PP
.BI "double exp10(double " x );
.br
.BI "double exp10m1(double " x );
.br
.BI "double exp2m1(double " x );
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.BR exp ()
function returns the value of
.RI e^ x ,
where
.I e
is the base of the natural logarithm.
.PP
The
.BR exp2 ()
function returns
.RI 2^ x .
.PP
The
.BR expm1 ()
function returns
.RI e^ x " \- 1.  It is computed in a way that is accurate even when "
.I x
is very close to zero \(em a case in which a direct
.BI exp( x )" \- 1"
would lose nearly all significant digits to catastrophic cancellation.
.PP
The C23 extensions
.BR exp10 (),
.BR exp10m1 (),
and
.BR exp2m1 ()
return
.RI 10^ x ,
.RI 10^ x " \- 1, and 2^" x " \- 1 respectively, the latter two preserving"
precision for small arguments in the same way as
.BR expm1 ().
.SH RETURN VALUE
On success the family of exponential functions returns the value
specified above.
.PP
If
.I x
is NaN the returned value is NaN.
.PP
If
.I x
is a positive infinity the value returned is positive infinity for
.BR exp (),
.BR exp2 (),
.BR exp10 (),
.BR expm1 (),
.BR exp2m1 (),
and
.BR exp10m1 ().
.PP
If
.I x
is a negative infinity the value returned is +0 for
.BR exp (),
.BR exp2 (),
and
.BR exp10 (),
and \-1 for
.BR expm1 (),
.BR exp2m1 (),
and
.BR exp10m1 ().
.PP
If the result overflows the range of representable values, positive
infinity is returned.  If the result underflows to zero, zero is
returned.  In both cases
.I errno
is set to
.BR ERANGE .
.SH ERRORS
.TP
.B ERANGE
A range error occurred: the magnitude of
.I x
is large enough that
.RI e^ x
overflows the
.I double
range, or so negative that
.RI e^ x
underflows to zero.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Computing the cumulative distribution function of an exponential
random variable:
.PP
.RS
.nf
#include <math.h>
double F(double x, double lambda) {
    /* 1 \- exp(\-lambda * x) — expm1 avoids cancellation near x=0 */
    return \-expm1(\-lambda * x);
}
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR log (3),
.BR pow (3),
.BR sinh (3),
.BR math (7)
.SH STANDARDS
C99, POSIX.1\-2001.  C23 added
.BR exp10 (),
.BR exp10m1 (),
and
.BR exp2m1 ().
